@startuml
!include style.puml

title PWasm WAL-Oriented Write Path (multi-transaction WAL)
caption Wizard Engine commit 8b262f4c24497bd2c5abe37c4b84c40dd4a97bf8, 2026-07-02.

actor Caller
participant "PWRegion" as PW
participant "RegionTransaction\n(write-behind cache)" as Txn
participant "MultiTxnWal\n(block 1 ring log)" as WAL
participant "Mapped region bytes" as Bytes
participant "BackendRegion" as BackendRegion

Caller -> PW : metadata/chunk update
PW -> Txn : writeU8/writeI16/writeU64/writeI64(addr, value)
Txn -> Txn : cache[addr] = CachedUpdate(value, width)\naddrs.put(addr) on first touch

Caller -> PW : operation reaches performCommit()
PW -> Txn : commit() : bool
note right of Txn
Clean-txn guard: commit() on a
non-dirty cache is a no-op (returns true).
end note

== 1. Buffer entries ==
Txn -> WAL : append(offset, value, width) for each cached addr
WAL -> WAL : pendingEntries.put(WalPendingEntry(...))

== 2. Commit point: one contiguous durable record ==
Txn -> WAL : commit() : txnSeq
WAL -> Bytes : reserveRecord() -> ring slot (wrap-around;\nlazy checkpoint + retry if the ring is full)
WAL -> Bytes : write TxnRecordHeader (magic/version/epoch/txnSeq)\n+ LogEntry[] + TxnCommitTrailer + FNV checksum
WAL -> BackendRegion : persistRange(record) -- COMMIT POINT
BackendRegion --> WAL : record durable
WAL -> WAL : activeRecords.put(...); activeBytes += len; nextTxnSeq++
WAL --> Txn : txnSeq (0 = failure)
note right of Txn
On txnSeq == 0 the commit fails: return false,
cache stays dirty (writes retained, not lost).
Surfaced as blankChunkHandle / false by
allocChunk() / freeChunk().
end note

== 3. Apply after-images to the region ==
Txn -> WAL : applyUpdate(offset, value, width) for each cached addr
WAL -> Bytes : writeAfterImage -- Pointer.store width-sized value
WAL -> BackendRegion : prepareChangedRange(offset, width)
Txn -> WAL : noteApplied(txnSeq)
WAL -> WAL : appliedSeqVolatile = txnSeq (if contiguous)

== 4. Best-effort checkpoint (publish durable floor) ==
Txn -> WAL : maybeCheckpoint() : bool
note right of WAL
Hybrid count-OR-occupancy policy, per-backend
thresholds chosen via checkpointCost():
  lag >= checkpointTxnThreshold, OR
  activeBytes >= checkpointFillPercent% of ringBytes
end note
alt checkpoint triggered
  WAL -> BackendRegion : persistChanges() -- after-images durable
  WAL -> Bytes : writeSuperblock(durableAppliedSeq = appliedSeqVolatile, epoch)
  WAL -> BackendRegion : persistRange(inactive superblock copy), then swap
  WAL -> WAL : durableAppliedSeq = targetSeq; reclaimAppliedRecords()
end
note right of Txn
A failed maybeCheckpoint() does NOT fail the
commit -- data stays WAL-recoverable; only a
Trace.OUT diagnostic is emitted.
end note

== 5. Clear cache in place ==
Txn -> Txn : cache.remove(addr) for each; addrs.clear()\n(reuses map + vector storage across commits)
Txn --> PW : true

@enduml
